  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Aurora Stack merchant, resident of the Promenade Ward, active during the Frozen Peace. Hainou mewei'Frostglass is best understood not through any single accomplishment but through the uses others made of what she provided. She discovered the Snowdrift-numb technique near the Bastion Apex — a method of aurora-channeling that permits navigation of ice-locked memory at the cost of progressive flipper degradation — and she found the Dreaming Tooth, a relic of disputed theological significance now held by Wake-Singer shamans at the Corpse Current, where it amplifies their blood-rituals. She wears practical silver-clasped robes embroidered with trade-routes that no longer exist. Her left flipper carries a permanent tremor; earlier accounts attribute this to frostbite sustained during the Apex expedition, while later sources cite cumulative damage from Snowdrift-numb practice. Both may be true.
    
    ## Role in the Promenade Ward's Founding
    
    Hainou's contribution to the Promenade Ward was logistical rather than heroic: supply lines, ice-record access, fire-core distribution channels — the infrastructure a colony requires before it can afford to produce heroes. She carved her initials into the foundation-stone of Light Ingjeizhi, the Ward's central spire, at its deepest level. Someone maintains them. She has not said who.
    
    ## The Consequences of Teaching
    
    She taught Summit-Lord Yahailong the Snowdrift-numb technique at Yahailong's request. Yahailong later used it to alter ice-memory, erasing the names of two families — Moqai and Xuelin — who froze when fire-cores were diverted to western perimeter defenses during the Ward's third winter. The ice retains both the original and the revision, as Snowdrift-numb alterations layer rather than replace. Hainou's role in providing the tool is documented; her knowledge of its application is not.
    
    She also mentored Plunge-Caller Oeichowei the Storm-Caller, who emerged as a tide-touched mystic under Hainou's guidance and went on to found the Pinnacle, a splinter faction that broke from Qingfu'spire. Hainou still sets aside fire-core tea on days Oeichowei ventures into the deep.
    
    ## Theological Contribution
    
    Cited in Aurora liturgical scholarship as the first commentator to identify the creation tradition's silence regarding the Glow-Fissure — an omission every subsequent theologian has been obliged to address.
    
    ## Standing
    
    Recognized as a stabilizing presence in Flipper Accord negotiations. Suspected by competitors of undisclosed knowledge of Nightshelf movements. She does not speak of what the ice showed her at Apex.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
